    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: `salutation` derived from optional `title`\n\nThe spec required composing `salutation = title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given. The app derives response fields via a MapStruct mapper over the persisted `Owner` entity, so `title` had to round-trip through storage.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (optional, `maxLength: 10`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema, and `salutation` (read-only) to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps `title` from the request DTO onto the entity and back onto the response DTO.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", ...)` plus a `salutation(Owner)` method returning `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is `null`/blank.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table. This was essential because the **test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`**, so the column has to exist in the SQL schema rather than being auto-created by Hibernate.\n\n**Result:** the new `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` (POST with `title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 GET returns `salutation=\"DR who\"`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
